I want to use a CICD workflow to read a requirement for a new feature in my PGT jira project.
Then the CICD orchestration implements it as defined by my templates.

observe
- get current baseline states
- review templates
- set up new feature branch
- set up new build id

plan / define
- write feature and test plans as described templates

act / execute
- write cwe compliant java code (jtest + publish)
- generate unit tests for new code only (jtest + publish)
- generate API test scernios to tets new feature (soatest mcp)

test
- deploy app with code coverage (docker)
- run generated API test (soatest + coverage + publish)

verify
- fix bugs or tests
- generate accountability report
- create PR

Now:
1. lets start by review existing workflows and repo contents to see what all is missing and still needs to be added to the repo/workflow
2. next letswork on writing the requirement in a way that the cicd pipeline can one-shot this task